  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader on iPhone, I want to scroll the last message of a page fully above the floating bottom controls, so that no text stays hidden behind the page arrows, the page number and the \"+\" button.\n\n### Observed (operator, device, 2026-11-12)\n- Reader, last page of a topic (page 3/3), scrolled to the very end: the last lines of the last message stay under the floating bottom controls (‹ ›, \"3 / 3\", \"+\"). The page cannot be scrolled further, so those lines can never be read.\n- Screenshot kept locally by the operator (it shows real member pseudos, so it is not attached).\n\n### Expected\nAt the end of the page, the last line of the last message (and its \"Message édité…\" trailer) sits above the bottom controls, with the usual margin. Same for the top, see #641.\n\n### Pointers\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/TopicReaderView.swift:73-81`: the web view ignores the vertical safe area and receives `obscured: proxy.safeAreaInsets`. Check that the bottom inset handed to the web view counts the floating controls of `ReaderPageControls.swift` (`.bottomBar` items, `:21-36`), not only the home indicator.\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/ReaderWebController+Scroll.swift`: how the obscured insets become the page's bottom padding or scroll inset.\n- Related: #641 (top), #820 (reader bars), #565 and #649 (pagers under the tab bar).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- On iPhone 18 Pro and iPad (iOS 27), portrait and landscape: scrolled to the end, the last line of the page is fully visible above the bottom controls.\n- A test fails without the fix: the bottom inset handed to the page is at least the height of the floating controls.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
